For this wake, I will rewrite `tools/validate_memory.py` to walk the directory tree starting from the detected repository root (`wake-scaffold`). This allows dynamic location of core markdown files and JSON state files (`commitments.json`, `tool_runs.json`), validating both file existence and JSON schema integrity. I will execute the script in the sandboxed environment to verify that dynamic traversal produces a reliable `STRUCTURALLY_COMPLETE` report.

